Unmodified upstream CPU shared library. No CUDA or GPU provider is required.

The library and required notices are embedded in Linux x86_64 builds. At
first inference they are materialized to a versioned user cache directory.
Existing library bytes are SHA-256 checked; writes use a unique temporary
file, fsync and atomic rename. No runtime download is performed. Other
architectures, unavailable caches, or load failures use the bundled
portable Rust inference backend and the same model instead.
